# GameHoverDetails: preview vs hover parity

When editing **GameHoverDetails** hover UI or settings preview:

- **`GameHoverDetailsHoverService`** defines the real popup. **`GameHoverDetailsSettingsView`** must stay visually and structurally aligned for titles, glyph chip column, width, block spacing, separators, and panel chrome.
- **Titles** — Game-art keys (`HoverFieldCatalog.IsGameArtImageField`: Icon, Cover Image, Background Image) have **no** title row in the hover (`TryAppendGameArtRow`). The settings preview must not show field titles for those keys when mirroring the hover (`ShowFieldTitleRow` / `ShowPreviewArt` paths).
- **Icon-only** — When **Icon** is the **only** selected field and the bitmap loads, the hover shows **Name** beside the 40 DIP icon (`ShowIconBesideGameNameRow` / `TryAppendGameArtRow` + `onlyIconSelected`); text uses `VerticalAlignment="Center"` next to the image.
- **Icons** — Inline catalog glyphs (Phosphor / Unicons / Huge Icons via `HoverIconStyle`) sit in a chip column sized by `HoverIconChipSizeDip` (default **32** DIP) with **10** DIP gap to text when `ShowFieldInlineIconsInHover` and the field is **not** game-art (`AppendTextDetailRow` / `AppendPlatformRow`). Glyph size is `HoverIconChipSizeDip` (default **32**). Chip box is `size + 2× HoverIconChipPaddingDip` (default padding **8**) so padding does not change the glyph. Chip corners come from `HoverIconChipShape` (`ResolveIconChipCornerRadius`: Circle default, Rectangle, Rounded, SoftRounded, Squircle, Arch, Tile, Leaf). `HideIconChipBackground` makes `HoverChromePalette.GlyphChipBackground` transparent (glyph only); style and color pickers are hidden then. With icons off, body is full width — no reserved empty column in the preview.
- **Stat row** — When titles and inline icons are both on, the hover uses one grid row: chip | stacked label + value (`ConfigureFieldLabelTextBlock` + body). Preview uses `ShowStatRowLayout`; do not use a full-width title row above the chip for that mode.
- **Separators** — `AppendFieldBlockSeparator` / preview `ShowTopSeparator` + `SeparatorMargin` using `SeparatorPadDip` (0.5× block spacing) and **`HoverChromePalette.Separator`** (divider hex, not the panel border). `HideFieldDividers` drops the 1px line (`Height` 0) but keeps the spacer margins. After a divider, preview must add the same **continuation top** as hover (`PreviewFieldTitleMargin` for title+value rows, `ContinuationRowOutermostMargin` on stat/chip/value-only/art roots) so space above and below the line both scale with `HoverFieldBlockSpacingDip`.
- **Settings** — Keep preview in sync with `HideFieldTitlesInHover`, `ShowFieldInlineIconsInHover`, `HideIconChipBackground`, `HideFieldDividers`, `HidePanelBorder`, `HoverChromeDividerHex`, `HoverBodyFontSize` / `HoverTitleFontSize` (line heights `18/13` and `14/10.5`), `HoverIconStyle` / `HoverIconChipSizeDip` / `HoverIconChipPaddingDip` / `HoverIconChipShape`, `HoverFieldBlockSpacingDip` / `HoverContentPaddingDip`, `UseGameBackground` / `HoverBackgroundStyle` (overview fanart + opacity-scaled #000000 tint, wider panel, height follows the field list like Regular; fanart `Stretch.UniformToFill` covers the panel while keeping aspect ratio, cropping overflow — typically the sides), `HoverChromeBackgroundOpacity`, `UseThemeChrome` / custom chrome (`HoverChromePalette`), and inner width relative to `HoverWidth` (`HoverContentPaddingDip` on each side of the preview list, default **14**; hover inset is **2×** that). Fanart must still cover the panel edge-to-edge under that padding (clip to the 8 DIP corner radius).

See **`src/GameHoverDetails/AGENTS.md`** (Preview vs hover parity) for the canonical checklist.
